Q: Efficient C++ way to shift a cv::Mat with OpenCV A: <p>I don't know if this is more performant, but certainly easy to code and understand. If you trust warpAffine to perform well, it should be ok.</p>
<pre><code>cv::Mat chans[3];

int channel = 0;
int offsetX = 100;
int offsetY = 100;

split(image, chans);

cv::Mat trans_mat = (cv::Mat_&lt;double&gt;(2, 3) &lt;&lt; 1, 0, offsetX, 0, 1, offsetY);

warpAffine(chans[channel], chans[channel], trans_mat, chans[channel].size(),
         cv::INTER_LINEAR,
         cv::BORDER_WRAP); // &lt;- this is the trick to shifting &amp; wrapping values

merge(chans, 3, image);
</code></pre>
<p>Seven year gone, but I'm just starting to use the OpenCV library :)</p>
